examples.setup:
What does this C program print? (Body of `main`, `stdio.h` included.)

```c
int a = 2, b = 3;
a = a + b;
b = a * b;
a = b - a;
printf("%d %d", a, b);
```

What does this C program print? (Body of `main`, `stdio.h` included.)

```c
int n = 739;
printf("%d %d %d", n / 100, n / 10 % 10, n % 10);
```

What does this C program print? (Body of `main`, `stdio.h` included.)

```c
int a = 0, b = 1;
if (a)
    if (b)
        printf("X");
else
    printf("Y");
printf("Z");
```

Short-circuit. What does this C program print? (Body of `main`.)

```c
int x = 0;
if (x != 0 && 10 / x > 2)
    printf("big");
else
    printf("safe");
```

What does this C program print? (Body of `main`, `stdio.h` included.)

```c
int i, count = 0;
for (i = 10; i > 0; i -= 3) {
    count++;
}
printf("%d %d", count, i);
```

What does this C program print?

```c
int f(int a, int b) {
    return a * 10 + b;
}

int main(void) {
    printf("%d", f(f(1, 2), 3));
    return 0;
}
```

How many times does `print` run, and in what order?

```python
for i in range(2):
    for j in range(5):
        print(i, j)
```

How many times does `count++` run? (Body of `main`.)

```c
int n = 6, count = 0;
for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++)
    for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++)
        count++;
```

A doubling inner loop, and two loops in a row. How many times does `c++` run in each? (Fragments of `main`.)

```c
/* A */ for (i = 0; i < 16; i++) for (j = 1; j < 16; j *= 2) c++;
/* B */ for (i = 0; i < 5; i++) c++;  for (j = 0; j < 7; j++) c++;
```

